{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedSimpleCycles"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P","text":"DirectedGraph"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The sequence holds the graph (a value), so iterating again gives the same cycles, and changing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the original graph afterwards changes nothing. The first "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"type":"text","text":" copies the graph’s rows and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"decomposes them, O(n + m). Unbounded, the time between consecutive cycles is O(n + m)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(Johnson), so c cycles take O((n + m)(c + 1)); with a bound k the whole enumeration takes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O((c + n)·k·d^k) for average degree d (Gupta–Suzumura)."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/cycles\/directedsimplecycles"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cycles\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Cycles\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Cycles\/ST"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships"}],"metadata":{"title":"DirectedSimpleCycles","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/gith